              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Adrianne Son-Hing"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Good tasting...but perhaps next time I'll use 1/2-3/4 packet of ranch, it was quite salty even when I added more yogurt and mayo. I'd recommend tasting it first at 1/2 packet and slowly adding more in.",
            "datePublished": "2012-09-25T02:32:29.273Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Dee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We were having crawfish today and I was looking for a dipping sauce that would compliment the meal. I found this recipe and was surprised to know I had all of the ingredients on hand. I made it exactly as stated, but added cayenne pepper and 4 dashes of hot sauce. It was very good. I will use it as a dipping sauce for crawfish, hot wings and veggies in the future. Thank you!",
            "datePublished": "2010-04-02T10:26:41.760Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kerplode"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I'm a BzzAgent, so I got some Hidden Valley Ranch packets for free! We made a recipe similar to this, but it was just sour cream, Hidden Valley Ranch, and we jazzed it up with some dill. Dip in pretzels and you've got a TASTY treat!",
            "datePublished": "2012-10-26T14:44:45.303Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Caramela"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very nice! First time, I used strained yogurt (usually found in stores as Greek-yogurt) and after 1 hour in the fridge it was ready for dippings! Second time, I used another brand of ranch which was way more salty, and the final product was not as expected, so a recommendation is to taste and adjust according to your needs and to the brand you use.",
            "datePublished": "2006-03-03T21:48:42.077Z"
          },
